[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:26:24Z","email":"42048994+jdwillmsen@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jake Willmsen"},"message":"chore(claude): make ask rules match flag-first invocations\n\nClaude Code matches everything before the first * literally, so an ask\nrule written as `kubectl delete*` misses `kubectl -n ns delete ...`, and\n`git push*` misses `git -C dir push --force`. Each cluster-mutating rule\nnow has `<prog> * <verb>` and `<prog> * <verb> *` companions, and the\ngit push rules take a `git *push*` prefix. A * in a Bash rule matches any\ntext including spaces, and mid-pattern wildcards only draw a startup\nwarning on allow rules. Checked with a glob run over flag-first\ninvocations: all prompt; plain feature-branch pushes and\n--force-with-lease still do not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5","tree":{"sha":"d37b77601dc62622e38bf1d94b6e869eee13d9d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdwlabs/apps/git/trees/d37b77601dc62622e38bf1d94b6e869eee13d9d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdwlabs/apps/git/commits/b6446ce476ba67c0e64dbd517e5195e17d3a7a2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42048994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jdwillmsen","id":42048994,"login":"jdwillmsen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDQ4OTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdwillmsen/repos","site_admi