,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Juyotal/rcm-copilot/commits/17d1ec5b3faa179cc6697db0559d3a0f8b7010e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-17T08:11:38Z","email":"cesarkamga3@gmail.com","name":"madaocesar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-17T08:11:38Z","email":"cesarkamga3@gmail.com","name":"madaocesar"},"message":"test(rag): integration tests for HybridRetriever\n\nAdds a 10-row in-memory fixture dataset and a fake engine that parses\nthe retriever''s two SQL strings and runs them in Python (cosine for the\nvector leg, plainto_tsquery-equivalent tokenization for FTS). This lets\nus exercise the full search() path including RRF fusion without\nstanding up Postgres + pgvector in CI.\n\nAsserts both spec-mandated behaviours:\n  - ''CO-4'' returns CARC-4 as the top result (FTS-driven)\n  - ''claim denied because of missing modifier'' returns CARC-4 (vector-driven)\nplus blank queries, top_k capping, metadata filter scoping, and a\nparametrized sweep of seven semantic routing cases.","tree":{"sha":"b32a70dd706c19a949a6a24534180d0a7ed0866b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Juyotal/rcm-copilot/git/trees/b32a70dd706c19a949a6a24534180d0a7ed0866b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Juyotal/rcm-copilot/git/commits/17d1ec5b3faa179cc6697db0559d3a0f8b7010e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82684537?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Juyotal/followi